<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 28,900 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 28,900 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 28,900 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 52,010 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			17,327	    16,135</p>
<p>    Import cargo			11,573	    35,875</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, one ship was expected to sail and five were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Chemicals		10,950	 Bakri Orbitor	21/8</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,354	 Johar		  17/8</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 20,000	 Iliad		   due</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,155	 Rong Jiang	    due</p>
<p>Vegoil		   18,600	 Kristal		 due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    70,000	 Chesapeak City     17/8</p>
<p>Gas oil		  36,000	 Al-Sabiyah	   19/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
